# Force LF line endings on checkout, everywhere, regardless of the checking-out
# machine's git configuration.
#
# GitHub's windows-latest runners ship Git preconfigured with core.autocrlf=true,
# which silently rewrites LF to CRLF in any file Git detects as text -- including
# inside Go source files, and inside multi-line raw string literals within them.
# Several files here (theme.go, render_html.go, search.go, among others) embed
# multi-line backtick-delimited strings whose exact byte content several tests
# compare against with golden-output string equality. Without this file, the
# same commit compiles to a subtly different binary on Windows than on Linux or
# macOS: embedded strings gain a \r before every \n, and any test asserting
# exact LF-terminated output fails there and only there.
*.go   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
